# Example sudoers grant for scripts/host-ops/pin-prod-sha (gr685985).
#
# Installed BY HAND on the session-MCP host(s) with visudo — no script
# installs it. <worker user> is the factory's deploy user; <owner> is the
# user that owns the prod watched checkout.
#
# 1. Install a root-owned, non-writable COPY of the helper OUTSIDE any
#    checkout the worker user can write (a grant on a file that user can
#    edit would let it run anything as <owner>):
#      install -o root -g wheel -m 0755 scripts/host-ops/pin-prod-sha \
#        /usr/local/libexec/precis/pin-prod-sha
#    and beside it a root-owned pin-prod-sha.conf with ONE line,
#      PROD_CHECKOUT=<absolute path of the prod watched checkout>
#    (the helper sources nothing else from the repo).
# 2. The grant allows that path with exactly ONE argument of 40 hex
#    characters (sudoers matches the argument list as a glob; no `*`):
<worker user> ALL=(<owner>) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/precis/pin-prod-sha [0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]
